.TH DIRNAME 1 "2026" "spicule" "spicule User Commands"
.SH NAME
dirname \- return the directory portion of a pathname
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B dirname
.I string
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B dirname
writes all but the final pathname component of
.IR string \|,
followed by a newline, to standard output.
.PP
Exactly one operand is accepted; no options are recognized.
.SH OPERANDS
.TP
.I string
A pathname.
.RS
.IP \(bu 2
An empty
.I string
produces a single
.BR . \|.
.IP \(bu 2
A
.I string
that names the root directory (one or more
.B /
characters, or a drive letter followed by
.B :
and one or more separators) produces that root unchanged, with any
repeated trailing separators collapsed to one.
.IP \(bu 2
A
.I string
with no directory component at all (no separator, and, for a
drive-qualified pathname, no separator after the drive letter and
colon) produces
.B .
for a plain pathname, or the bare drive prefix (such as
.BR C: )
for a drive-qualified one.
.IP \(bu 2
Otherwise, the result is
.I string
with its final pathname component, and the separator(s) immediately
before it, removed.
.RE
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Successful completion.
.TP
.B 1
Writing the result to standard output failed.
.TP
.B 2
An operand count other than exactly one was given.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR basename (1),
.BR pathchk (1)
